---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Navigate an explicitly supplied complete descriptor set, or compare schema worlds

Usage: pse inspect schema [OPTIONS] --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR> [DECLARATION]

Arguments:
  [DECLARATION]  Exact schema declaration name or returned descriptor address; omission lists files

Options:
  -C <checkout>

      --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR>
          Complete descriptor set including imports
      --compare-with <COMPARE_WITH>
          Compare the selected current bundle with an explicit original baseline
      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --semantic-file <SEMANTIC_FILE>
          Original file to assess semantically; repeat for a bounded explicit selection
      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --semantic-policy <SEMANTIC_POLICY>
          Available native semantic policy; acquired options cannot nominate native coverage [possible values: core, developer-evidence, recorded-result, native-usage]
  -h, --help
          Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Navigate an explicitly supplied complete descriptor set, or compare schema worlds

Usage: pse inspect schema [OPTIONS] --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR> [DECLARATION]

Arguments:
  [DECLARATION]
          Exact schema declaration name or returned descriptor address; omission lists files

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR>
          Complete descriptor set including imports

      --compare-with <COMPARE_WITH>
          Compare the selected current bundle with an explicit original baseline

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --semantic-file <SEMANTIC_FILE>
          Original file to assess semantically; repeat for a bounded explicit selection

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --semantic-policy <SEMANTIC_POLICY>
          Available native semantic policy; acquired options cannot nominate native coverage

          Possible values:
          - core:               Understand core metadata only; native source coverage remains unavailable
          - developer-evidence: Current independent-host developer evidence source policy and generated coverage
          - recorded-result:    Original recorded-result observation metadata for the explicitly selected result file
          - native-usage:       Source-owned dependency usage and its shared native context declarations

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
